          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "For every nonempty set $X$, every relation $R$ entire on $X$, and every $a \\in X$, there is a function $x : \\mathbb{N} \\to X$ with $x_0 = a$ and $x_n \\mathbin{R} x_{n+1}$ for every $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$.",
