        {
          "supplier": "thm-emg-local-classical-charged-scalar-development",
          "carrier": "items/thm-emg-local-classical-charged-scalar-development.md",
          "status": "Current authored supplier inspected after its drained normal-evolution, finite-Sobolev, gauge-uniqueness and charged-derivative repairs; draft status is not a missing proof.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Require $F_\\Sigma|_{T\\Sigma}=d_\\Sigma A_\\Sigma$, $\\pi_i=(\\mathcal D_i\\varphi_0)=\\partial_i\\varphi_0-i\\lambda A_{\\Sigma,i}\\varphi_0$, and $A(n)=0$. Fix a smooth positive reference metric $\\gamma$ and the product comparison metric $\\bar g=-(dx^0)^2+\\gamma$ near the initial slice. The harmonic-gauge vector is $H^a:=g^{bc}(\\Gamma(g)^a{}_{bc}-\\Gamma(\\bar g)^a{}_{bc})$; use the initial jet from [[lem-emg-fixed-smooth-background-harmonic-data]]:\n\n$$g_{ij}=h_{ij},\\quad g_{00}=-1,\\quad g_{0i}=0,\\quad \\partial_0g_{ij}=2K_{ij},\\quad \\partial_0g_{00}=-2\\operatorname{tr}_hK,\\quad \\partial_0g_{0i}=h_{ij}h^{k\\ell}(\\Gamma(h)^j{}_{k\\ell}-\\Gamma(\\gamma)^j{}_{k\\ell}).$$\n\nLet $D$ be the Levi–Civita derivative of $h$, $\\tau=\\operatorname{tr}_hK$, and $T=T^{\\mathrm{EM}}+T^\\varphi$ be evaluated on the complete initial data. Define $j^0:=-n_aj^a$ in the normal frame and assume the sourced Maxwell and total-stress Einstein constraints\n\n$$D_i b^i=0,\\qquad D_i e^i=\\mu_0j^0,\\qquad R(h)+\\tau^2-|K|_h^2=2\\Lambda+2\\kappa T(n,n),\\qquad (\\operatorname{div}_hK)(X)-D_X\\tau=\\kappa T(n,X)\\quad(X\\in T\\Sigma),$$\n\nwhere $(\\operatorname{div}_hK)(X)=h^{ij}(D_{\\partial_i}K)(\\partial_j,X)$, $\\kappa=8\\pi G_N/c^4$, and $K(X,Y)=g(\\nabla_Xn,Y)$. The constraint expressions are interpreted using their continuous representatives at the stated Sobolev orders. On the reduced coordinate domain require $g^{00}<0$ and the inverse spatial block $(g^{ij})$ to be positive definite. The real first-order state consists of the metric variables $(g_{ab},p_{ab},q_{abi})$ relative to a fixed smooth background, the six Maxwell variables $(e_i,b_i)$, the three potential components $A_i$, and the real and imaginary parts of $\\varphi,\\pi_0,\\pi_i$. For fixed reference scales $L_0>0$ metres and $F_0>0$ tesla, replace each first metric derivative $v$ and each $\\pi_a$ by $L_0v$ and $L_0\\pi_a$, each $e_i,b_i$ by $e_i/F_0,b_i/F_0$, and each $A_i$ by $A_i/(L_0F_0)$; $g_{ab}$ and $\\varphi$ are already dimensionless. These fixed invertible rescalings make the componentwise real Sobolev state dimensionless and add no equations. Let $u_0$ be the resulting state in the sense of [[def-emg-periodic-high-sobolev-state]], and suppose its continuous range is a compact $K_0$ contained in the interior of a compact $K_1$ inside an open admissible state set $O$, with $\\|u_0\\|_{H^s}\\le R$ and $R\\ge0$. The coefficient maps are smooth on $O$, the potential range lies in $\\mathcal U$, and the combined time matrix is positive definite throughout $O$.\n\nThen there is $T_*>0$ and a local solution on $(-T_*,T_*)\\times\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$ of the full Einstein, sourced Maxwell, and classical charged-scalar equations. Its first-order metric and matter state has the $L^\\infty H^s\\cap C H^{s-1}$ regularity of [[thm-emg-symmetric-hyperbolic-research-supplier]]; the metric satisfies $g\\in L^\\infty H^{s+1}\\cap C H^s$ and $\\partial_0g\\in L^\\infty H^s\\cap C H^{s-1}$, while $F,\\pi,A_i\\in L^\\infty H^s\\cap C H^{s-1}$ and $\\varphi\\in L^\\infty H^{s+1}\\cap C H^s$. The constraints and first-order metric, scalar, and potential compatibility conditions propagate. Smooth data give a smooth development on the same local interval.\n\nMore generally, let $\\Sigma$ be any smooth oriented three-manifold without boundary. Prescribe smooth $h$ positive definite, symmetric $K$, spatial vector fields $e,b$, a global one-form $A_\\Sigma$, a complex scalar $\\varphi_0$, and its independent normal derivative $\\pi_n$. Define $F_\\Sigma$ by the same $h,e,b$ convention in local positively oriented orthonormal frames, without requiring a global frame. Require $F_\\Sigma|_{T\\Sigma}=d_\\Sigma A_\\Sigma$, $\\pi_i=\\mathcal D_i\\varphi_0$, $A(n)=0$, and the sourced Maxwell and total-stress Einstein constraints displayed above at every point of $\\Sigma$.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "AC_omega and DC; integer s>=5, h and phi_0 in H^(s+1), remaining complete data in H^s, strict compact admissible state range and positive time matrix; both branches use mathcal D for charged compatibility, D only for spatial Levi-Civita; invariant sourced Maxwell and total-stress Einstein constraints. General smooth data obey the same charged compatibility, with smooth local development and geometric uniqueness after temporal-gauge restoration.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Complete authored local proof used at its exact hypotheses; this consumer does not create an independent acceptance stamp.",
          "consumer_use": "Supplies periodic finite-Sobolev development, smooth persistence, and the full smooth local development and isometry-plus-real-gauge uniqueness under the displayed complete data; no additional lambda A phi=0 condition."
